<think>Okay, so I have this problem here about rolling a fair die and figuring out which of the given options is most likely. Let me try to break it down step by step. First off, I know that a standard die has six faces, numbered from 1 to 6. Since it's fair, each face has an equal probability of landing face up, right? That means each number from 1 through 6 has a 1/6 chance of being the outcome, or probability of 1/6. Since there are six equally likely outcomes, each one is about 16.67% likely if I convert that fraction to a percentage in my head. Hmm, yeah, 1 divided by 6 is approximately 0.1667. Okay, so each number has that same probability. Now, the question is asking which of the options A through E is the most likely result for x, the number that comes up when the die is rolled. Let me look at each option one by one and analyze them based on probability.

